This extension adds State of Decay 2 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox (Game Pass)[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs UE4SS Script-LogicMod Combo mod with both a "Content" and a "Binaries" folder to the "StateOfDecay2" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs UE Sortable Pak mod with a ".pak" file to the "LOCALAPPDATA\StateOfDecay2\Saved\Paks" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs Root Folder mod with a top-level folder such as "StateOfDecay2", "Engine" or "Content" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs Config (Local AppData) mod with a config file such as "engine.ini" or "game.ini".[/*]
[*]Installs Saves (Local AppData) mod with a ".sav" file.[/*]
[*]Installs Cooked mod with a file or folder named "Cooked" to the "{localAppData}\StateOfDecay2\Saved" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs SoD2 Mod Manager itself, recognised by a file or folder named "modintegrator.exe".[/*]
[*]Installs Binaries (Engine Injector) mod with anything unrecognised with no pak file to the "StateOfDecay2\Binaries\Win64" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

